{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-346495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(4{x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-346495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4{x}^{2}+3\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(4{x}^{2}+3)(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(4{x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-(4{x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(4{x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =-(4{x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=8D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(4{x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-(4{x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-(4{\\pi }^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +8\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi )-(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+8(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =(4{\\pi }^{2}+3-8)-(-3+8) \\\\  & =4{\\pi }^{2}-5-5 \\\\  & =4{\\pi }^{2}-10\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-346495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80c343f6220b0841b31908b283c2be395b14bd2eec8b7615fa78b6728d13d4ac"} {"question" "q-346495" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-346495" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\pi^2-10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5{x}^{2}+7\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=10x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(5{x}^{2}+7)(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(10x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=10D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-(5{x}^{2}+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-(5{\\pi }^{2}+7)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +10\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +10\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi )-(-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+10(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =(5{\\pi }^{2}+7-10)-(-7+10) \\\\  & =5{\\pi }^{2}-3-3 \\\\  & =5{\\pi }^{2}-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80c343f6220b0841b31908b283c2be395b14bd2eec8b7615fa78b6728d13d4ac"} {"question" "q-352000" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352000" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\pi^2-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=12x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(6{x}^{2})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(12x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-12\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-12\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-12(-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-12D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={[6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+12x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{2}-12)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{2}-12\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80c343f6220b0841b31908b283c2be395b14bd2eec8b7615fa78b6728d13d4ac"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352029" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}\\pi^2-12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{e}({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡(4)}(${{field-1}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int {log}_{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{4}⁡x)(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{4}⁡x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{4}⁡x-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(x{log}_{4}⁡x-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2x{log}_{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{2x}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}+\\frac{2x}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}({ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{4}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}({ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2)]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}({ln}^{2}⁡e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+2)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}({ln}^{2}⁡1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}(1-2+2)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}(0-0+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}-\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}(\\,e-2\\,)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80c343f6220b0841b31908b283c2be395b14bd2eec8b7615fa78b6728d13d4ac"} {"question" "q-352123" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352123" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}2({log}_{3}⁡(2x))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡(3)}(${{field-1}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{3}⁡(2x))^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2({log}_{3}⁡(2x))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{3}⁡(2x))}^{2}(2x)-\\int (2x)(\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x{({log}_{3}⁡(2x))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡(2x))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡(2x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2({log}_{3}⁡(2x))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =2x{({log}_{3}⁡(2x))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x{log}_{3}⁡(2x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =2x{({log}_{3}⁡(2x))}^{2}-\\frac{4x{log}_{3}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{4x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2x{ln}^{2}⁡(2x)}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+\\frac{4x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡(2x)-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+4)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{4D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡(2x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{e/2}2({log}_{3}⁡(2x))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡(2x)-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+4)]}_{1/2}^{e/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{e/2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡e-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+4)-\\frac{1/2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2{ln}^{2}⁡1-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{e/2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(2-4+4)-\\frac{1/2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(0-0+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(\\,e-2\\,)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80c343f6220b0841b31908b283c2be395b14bd2eec8b7615fa78b6728d13d4ac"} {"question" "q-352124" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c41"} {"question" "q-352124" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029309/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea8be05cd86c20038688bda011d26bbac4bc87784b50a5a13ab37954ff0a4c